<title>UK: HORSE RACING-ENGLISH 1,000 GUINEAS RESULT.</title>
<headline>HORSE RACING-ENGLISH 1,000 GUINEAS RESULT.</headline>
<dateline>NEWMARKET, England 1997-05-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Result of the English</p>
<p>1,000 Guineas, a group one race for three-year-old fillies, run</p>
<p>over one mile (1.6 km) on Sunday:</p>
<p>1. Sleepytime  5-1 (ridden by Kieren Fallon)</p>
<p>2. Oh Nellie  50-1 (Willie Ryan)</p>
<p>3. Dazzle     16-1 (John Reid)</p>
<p>15 ran.</p>
<p>Favourite: Pas de Reponse (5-2) finished fourth. Distances: four lengths, three quarters of a length.</p>
<p>Winner owned by Greenbay Stables Limited and trained at Newmarket by Henry Cecil.</p>
<p>Value to winner: 104,730 pounds sterling ($169,000)</p>
</text>
